[2.84,"o","\r\n"]
[2.88,"o","\u001b[1mwp-doctor 0.2.0, WordPress 6.5.2\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.92,"o","\r\n"]
[2.96,"o","\u001b[1m\u001b[31mCRITICAL (3)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3,"o","  [config.salts.default] Authentication keys and salts are missing, sample text or repeated\r\n"]
[3.04,"o","    AUTH_KEY: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.08,"o","    SECURE_AUTH_KEY: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.12,"o","    LOGGED_IN_KEY: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.16,"o","    NONCE_KEY: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.2,"o","    AUTH_SALT: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.24,"o","    SECURE_AUTH_SALT: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.28,"o","    LOGGED_IN_SALT: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.32,"o","    NONCE_SALT: still the sample placeholder text\r\n"]
[3.36,"o","    Fix: Generate fresh random values at https://api.wordpress.org/secret-key/1.1/salt/ and paste all eight define() lines over the old ones in wp-config.php. Everyone is logged out once when you do.\r\n"]
[3.4,"o","  [disk.leftovers.web] Database dumps or copies of wp-config.php are likely downloadable from the web root\r\n"]
[3.44,"o","    matching_files: 1\r\n"]
[3.48,"o","    scan_incomplete: false\r\n"]
[3.52,"o","    file_1: backup-2026-11-01.sql\r\n"]
[3.56,"o","    file_1_bytes: 54\r\n"]
[3.6,"o","    Fix: Move each file out of the web root (or delete it). If a copy of wp-config.php or a dump was reachable, treat the database password and the keys and salts in it as exposed and change them.\r\n"]
[3.64,"o","  [sec.uploads.php] PHP files in the uploads directory\r\n"]
[3.68,"o","    php_files: 1\r\n"]
[3.72,"o","    empty_index_stubs_ignored: 0\r\n"]
[3.76,"o","    scan_incomplete: false\r\n"]
[3.8,"o","    uploads_location_unconfirmed: the upload_path option, which can move the uploads directory, could not be read: database connection failed: Could not connect to the database (error 2002): php_network_getaddresses: getaddrinfo for [redacted] failed: nodename nor servname provided, or not known\r\n"]
[3.84,"o","    file_1: wp-content/uploads/2026/11/cache.php\r\n"]
[3.88,"o","    file_1_bytes: 56\r\n"]
[3.92,"o","    Fix: Uploads should hold media only. Open each file; if you did not put it there, treat the site as compromised: remove the file, work out how it arrived from the access logs, change the passwords and the keys and salts, and stop the web server from running PHP in the uploads directory.\r\n"]
[3.96,"o","\r\n"]
[4,"o","\u001b[1m\u001b[33mWARNING (5)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.04,"o","  [config.debug.enabled] Debugging is likely switched on for a live site\r\n"]
[4.08,"o","    WP_DEBUG: on\r\n"]
[4.12,"o","    WP_DEBUG_DISPLAY: on\r\n"]
[4.16,"o","    WP_DEBUG_LOG: off\r\n"]
[4.2,"o","    Fix: On a live site set WP_DEBUG to false in wp-config.php; WP_DEBUG_DISPLAY and WP_DEBUG_LOG only apply while it is on.\r\n"]
[4.24,"o","    Keep debugging on only in a development copy.\r\n"]
[4.28,"o","  [config.perms.wpconfig] wp-config.php can be read or changed by other accounts on the server\r\n"]
[4.32,"o","    path: wp-config.php\r\n"]
[4.36,"o","    mode: 0644\r\n"]
[4.4,"o","    Fix: Run `chmod 640 wp-config.php`, or `chmod 600 wp-config.php` when the web server runs as the file owner. If the database password may have been read by someone else, change it. If others could write the file, compare it with a known good copy before trusting it.\r\n"]
[4.44,"o","  [perf.objectcache.missing] No persistent object cache is installed\r\n"]
[4.48,"o","    expected_file: wp-content/object-cache.php\r\n"]
[4.52,"o","    found: false\r\n"]
[4.56,"o","    Fix: If the host offers Redis or Memcached, install an object cache plugin that provides wp-content/object-cache.php. Small sites with little traffic may not need one.\r\n"]
[4.6,"o","  [sec.code.obfuscated] PHP files likely run obfuscated code\r\n"]
[4.64,"o","    php_files_examined: 8\r\n"]
[4.68,"o","    files_flagged: 1\r\n"]
[4.72,"o","    scan_incomplete: false\r\n"]
[4.76,"o","    file_1: wp-content/themes/example-theme/functions.php\r\n"]
[4.8,"o","    file_1_line: 3\r\n"]
[4.84,"o","    file_1_code: eval() of base64_decode()\r\n"]
[4.88,"o","    Fix: Open each file at the line given. Code that decodes a hidden string and runs it is a common form of injected malware, and plugins and themes seldom need it. Compare the file with a clean copy from where it came from: WordPress itself, or the plugin or theme download. If the code is not in the clean copy, treat the site as compromised: replace the file, change the passwords and the keys and salts, and look for how it was added.\r\n"]
[4.92,"o","  [sec.plugins.unknown] PHP in the plugins directory likely belongs to no plugin\r\n"]
[4.96,"o","    directory: wp-content/plugins\r\n"]
[5,"o","    entries_listed: 3\r\n"]
[5.04,"o","    flagged: 1\r\n"]
[5.08,"o","    scan_incomplete: false\r\n"]
[5.12,"o","    entry_1: wp-content/plugins/wp-zxq\r\n"]
[5.16,"o","    entry_1_reason: folder with PHP but no file with a Plugin Name header\r\n"]
[5.2,"o","    entry_1_php_files: 1\r\n"]
[5.24,"o","    entry_1_php_newest: 2026-11-08 13:16 UTC\r\n"]
[5.28,"o","    Fix: Look at each entry listed. WordPress loads a plugin only from a .php file with a `Plugin Name:` header at the top of its folder, so this code does not run as a plugin, yet anyone can request it over the web. A folder nested one level too deep (wp-content/plugins/name/name/) is a failed install: delete it and install the plugin again. Otherwise, if you did not put the code there, move it out of the web root to inspect it and treat the site as compromised: change the passwords and the keys and salts, and look for how it was added.\r\n"]
[5.32,"o","\r\n"]
[5.36,"o","\u001b[1m\u001b[36mINFO (2)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.4,"o","  [config.fileedit.enabled] The theme and plugin code editor is likely enabled\r\n"]
[5.44,"o","    DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT: not set to true in wp-config.php\r\n"]
[5.48,"o","    Fix: Add this line to wp-config.php above the line that loads wp-settings.php:\r\n"]
[5.52,"o","    define( 'DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true );\r\n"]
[5.56,"o","  [disk.uploads.size] Size of the uploads directory\r\n"]
